cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the references listed in the README (in particular Madej et al. 2017 for the Compton kernel and Gunasekera et al. 2025 for Cloudy)."
title: "DAO: A New and Public Non-Relativistic Reflection Model"
abstract: >-
  We present DAO, a new and public reflection model that computes rest-frame
  reflection spectra from accretion disks in X-ray binaries and active galactic
  nuclei. The code is built on three pillars: (i) the photoionization code
  Cloudy C25, which provides a comprehensive and up-to-date treatment of all
  relevant atomic processes, including line emission via the escape-probability
  formalism; (ii) the exact quantum-electrodynamic Compton redistribution
  kernel, which fully accounts for angle- and energy-dependent scattering
  rather than relying on the angle-averaged Gaussian or Fokker-Planck
  approximations adopted by existing reflection codes; and (iii) cubic Bezier
  interpolants for the formal solution of the radiative transfer equation, a
  monotonicity-preserving short-characteristics scheme that avoids spurious
  numerical oscillations. We investigate the spectral dependence on key
  physical parameters and benchmark the results against the publicly available
  table models of the widely used reflionx and xillver codes.
type: software
